[{:adr/consequences "{:isolation \"per-agent child-repo checkouts fully isolated; one agent's WIP cannot block another's west update\", :cost \"child repos duplicated per agent (disk/bandwidth) — mitigated by --fetch smart + shallow + DataLad/B2 for heavy\", :cannot_fix \"upstream force-push effects (origin/main force-rewrite, child-remote force-rewrite pin rollback) — worktree layout cannot prevent these; requires the CLAUDE.md force-push ban upstream\"}", :adr/authoritative_for ["how an agent isolates west child-repo checkouts: create the git worktree OUTSIDE the superproject root and run `west init -l manifest` inside it to fix topdir" "the failure mode of worktrees under .claude/worktrees/ (inside super): west walks up to the superproject's .west/ and treats the superproject as topdir, so west update lands in the shared orgs/ and collides with other agents' WIP" "WEST_TOPDIR env-var override does NOT fix this (.west/ discovery wins); only outside-root + init -l works"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "west-worktree-topdir", :adr/related ["CLAUDE.md" "90-docs/adr/2606241600-shallow-depth1-git-default.edn" "90-docs/adr/2606272237-manifest-workflow-single-entry-commit.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607010930-clj-wgsl-migration.edn"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607011345-agent-worktree-west-topdir-fix", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-01", :adr/body "# ADR-2607011345: Agent worktrees must fix west topdir (outside superproject root + `west init -l manifest`)\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-01\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n\n## Context\n\nMultiple agents (codex sessions, cleanup fleet, etc.) work on the superproject\nconcurrently. To avoid disturbing each other's working tree, the natural move is\nfor each agent to use its own `git worktree`. However, during the clj-wgsl\nmigration session, an agent working in a `.claude/worktrees/<name>` worktree ran\n`west update kami-webgpu` and observed:\n\n- the child repo did **not** materialise inside the worktree (`orgs/...` absent),\n- instead a **different agent's** uncommitted `M src/kami/dance.cljc` in the\n  superproject-main checkout was reported as a dirty blocker, and\n- `west update` skipped / failed on repos the main checkout had WIP in.\n\nRoot cause: **west resolves `topdir` by walking up from CWD looking for a\n`.west/` directory.** A `git worktree` created *under* the superproject root\n(the default `.claude/worktrees/<name>` location) is a subdirectory of the\nsuperproject, so the upward walk finds the superproject's own `.west/` and west\nconcludes `topdir = <superproject root>`. All `west update` / `west list` /\nchild-repo checkouts then target the **superproject's** `orgs/` — shared across\nevery agent — re-introducing the exact WIP collision the worktree was meant to\nisolate.\n\n`WEST_TOPDIR` env-var override does **not** fix this (`.west/` discovery wins),\nand `west init -l manifest` inside the nested worktree refuses with\n\"already initialized in <superproject>\" (it sees the superproject's `.west/`).\n\n## Decision\n\n**An agent that needs to run `west` in its own worktree must (a) create the\nworktree *outside* the superproject root (a sibling path), and (b) run\n`west init -l manifest` inside it to mint a worktree-local `.west/` that fixes\n`topdir` to that worktree.**\n\n```bash\ngit worktree add -b <agent-branch> /tmp/root-<agent-name> origin/main\ncd /tmp/root-<agent-name>\nwest init -l manifest          # worktree-local .west/ → topdir fixed here\nwest update --fetch smart <repo>\n```\n\nWorktrees created under `.claude/worktrees/` (inside the superproject) are fine\nfor **doc/script/manifest-only edits that never invoke `west`**, but must not be\nused for child-repo work.\n\n### Verified (2026-07-01)\n\n| setup | `west topdir` returns | `west update` lands in |\n|---|---|---|\n| worktree under `.claude/worktrees/` (inside super) | superproject root | superproject `orgs/` (shared — WRONG) |\n| worktree under `/tmp/...` (outside super) + `west init -l manifest` | the worktree | worktree `orgs/` (isolated — CORRECT) |\n\n`WEST_TOPDIR=<worktree> west topdir` still returned the superproject root —\nenv-var override is not a fix; only the outside + `init -l` combo works.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Each agent's child-repo checkouts are fully isolated; one agent's uncommitted\n  WIP can no longer block another agent's `west update`.\n- Cost: child repos are duplicated per agent (disk/bandwidth). Mitigated by\n  `--fetch smart` + shallow default; heavy repos stay on DataLad/B2.\n- **Does not prevent upstream force-push effects**: `origin/main` force-rewrites\n  and child-repo remote force-rewrites (pin rollback, `upload-pack: not our ref`)\n  are upstream problems no worktree layout can fix. Those require the\n  force-push ban already in CLAUDE.md to be honoured upstream.\n- CLAUDE.md \"リポジトリ構成\" section gains a subsection recording this rule.\n\n## Related\n\n- `CLAUDE.md` §リポジtori構成 / \"agent 専用 worktree で west を動かすときの topdir 固定\"\n- `90-docs/adr/2606241600-shallow-depth1-git-default.edn`\n- `90-docs/adr/2606272237-manifest-workflow-single-entry-commit.edn` (force-push ban)\n- `90-docs/adr/2607010930-clj-wgsl-migration.edn` (the session that surfaced this)", :adr/decision "{:rule \"agent worktrees that run west must be created OUTSIDE the superproject root (sibling path) and run `west init -l manifest` inside to mint a worktree-local .west/ fixing topdir\", :recipe [\"git worktree add -b <branch> /tmp/root-<agent> origin/main\" \"cd /tmp/root-<agent>\" \"west init -l manifest\" \"west update --fetch smart <repos>\"], :nested_worktree_scope \"worktrees under .claude/worktrees/ are OK for doc/script/manifest-only edits that never invoke west; never for child-repo work\", :verified {:inside_super \"west topdir = superproject root; west update lands in shared orgs/ (WRONG)\", :outside_super_plus_init \"west topdir = the worktree; west update lands in worktree orgs/ (CORRECT)\"}}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:source \"clj-wgsl migration session 2026-07-01: west update in a .claude/worktrees/ worktree did not check out child repos into the worktree; instead it hit another agent's WIP in the superproject-main checkout\", :root_cause \"west resolves topdir by walking up from CWD for a .west/ dir; a worktree under .claude/worktrees/ is a subdirectory of the superproject, so the walk finds the superproject's .west/ and west treats the superproject as topdir — all west operations target the shared orgs/\", :non_fixes [\"WEST_TOPDIR env-var override (returned super root anyway)\" \"west init -l manifest inside nested worktree (refuses: already initialized in super)\"], :risk \"agent worktrees give false isolation; west work silently lands in the shared superproject checkout, colliding with other agents' WIP and making west update skip/fail on dirty repos\"}", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607011345: Agent worktrees must fix west topdir (outside superproject root + west init -l manifest)", :adr/source-format "edn"}]